title: oiler_intro
---
<<present_speaker "npc_oiler">>
<<portrait_clip "talking">>
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "p1_stabilizer_received")>>
    Oiler: Knee holding? Good. Sit on the bench if you need to. It's mine, but I'm not using it.
    -> Where did the goblins go?
        Oiler: East, to the gate stack. The checkpoint there won't pass you. You're not on anybody's list.
        Oiler: The cartographers work the drains under the market. If there's a way round, they've drawn it.
    -> Where are the cartographers?
        Oiler: Down the drain cover by the news board. Mind the sump. It isn't water.
    -> ⟨move on⟩
<<else>>
    Oiler: Hold still. That knee's on crooked. Who put you together, a man in a hurry?
    -> He's dead. Goblins came for me.
        <<jump oiler_intro__repair>>
    -> I'm fine.
        Oiler: You're walking like a shopping cart. Hold still.
        <<jump oiler_intro__repair>>
    -> ⟨keep walking⟩
<<endif>>
===

title: oiler_intro__repair
---
<<present_speaker "npc_oiler">>
<<portrait_clip "inspecting">>
Oiler: ...A shim and some grease. It'll hold until something hits it.
<<command "world.set_flag" "p1_stabilizer_received" true>>
Oiler: Goblins, you said. Four of them came up the service stair at dawn with a crate. They went east.
Oiler: The checkpoint won't pass you. Ask the cartographers in the drains; they know every pipe under this street.
-> ⟨thank him⟩
===

title: news_board_lab_incident
---
Drain Market Bulletin: ▸ FIRE IN A BASEMENT ON CULVERT ROW. ONE DEAD, AN UNLICENSED RESEARCHER. NO OTHER DAMAGE.
-> ⟨read further⟩
    <<jump news_board_lab_incident__1>>
-> ⟨walk away⟩
===

title: news_board_lab_incident__1
---
Drain Market Bulletin: ▸ RESIDENTS ARE REMINDED THAT UNLICENSED RESEARCH IS A FIRE HAZARD.
Drain Market Bulletin: ▸ GATE SIX: DELAYED. SOUP: TUESDAYS.
-> ⟨leave the board to its work⟩
===

title: alice_station
---
<<present_speaker "npc_alice">>
<<portrait_clip "speaking">>
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "bob_field_survey_received")>>
    Alice: Bob has the last reading. Three days, closed. The line's down; my hatch comes up behind the news board.
    -> What's on Bob's sheet?
        Alice: The old drains past his end. They go under the checkpoint. Nobody's walked them since the official map was printed.
    -> ⟨leave⟩
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "alice_route_note_carried")>>
    Alice: Four-one-seven, and the word is "bramble". If he doesn't ask for the word, it isn't Bob.
    -> ⟨go⟩
<<else>>
    Alice: Don't step in front of the instrument. ...You're not from the market. You're not from anywhere, are you.
    -> Goblins came this way with a crate.
        <<jump alice_station__goblins>>
    -> What are you measuring?
        Alice: The drains. Bob holds the staff at the far end and I read it from here. Three days of readings. If either of us moves, we start again.
    -> Why don't you shout to Bob?
        Alice: Every drain in this town comes up in the market. Somebody is always listening.
    -> ⟨step back⟩
<<endif>>
===

title: alice_station__goblins
---
<<present_speaker "npc_alice">>
<<portrait_clip "speaking">>
Alice: They came through at dawn. Four of them, and the crate. East, past Bob's end.
Alice: Bob has those drains on his sheet. Take him my last reading: four-one-seven. He'll ask for a word. The word is "bramble".
<<command "world.set_flag" "alice_route_note_carried" true>>
Alice: Take a copy of my map too. It's better than the one they sell upstairs.
-> ⟨take the map⟩
===

title: bob_station
---
<<present_speaker "npc_bob">>
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "bob_field_survey_received")>>
    Bob: Past my end it's dry for a hundred paces, then it isn't. Keep to the left wall.
    -> ⟨go⟩
<<elseif condition("world.flag_set", "alice_route_note_carried")>>
    Bob: Alice sent you? What's the word?
    -> "Bramble." The reading is four-one-seven.
        <<jump bob_station__reading>>
    -> The reading is four-one-seven.
        Bob: Anybody can say a number. What's the word?
    -> ⟨make up a number⟩
        Bob: Ha. She'd never read a six from there. Who sent you, really?
    -> ⟨leave⟩
<<else>>
    Bob: Don't stand there. You're between me and Alice. Well, between me and a wall, and Alice is behind the wall.
    -> What are you doing?
        Bob: Holding a stick very still. Alice reads it from her end. It's harder than it looks.
    -> ⟨leave him to it⟩
<<endif>>
===

title: bob_station__reading
---
<<present_speaker "npc_bob">>
Bob: Four-one-seven. That closes it. Three days. She'll take the line down now.
<<give_item "fieldsurvey" 1>>
<<command "world.set_flag" "bob_field_survey_received" true>>
Bob: Here, take my sheet. The drains past my end run under the checkpoint. If you want the goblins, that's where the crate went.
-> ⟨take the survey⟩
===

title: eve_drain_pipe
---
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "bob_field_survey_received")>>
    Eve: You carried it. Three days I sat by this pipe, and they used a robot.
    -> ⟨walk on⟩
<<else>>
    Eve: Shh. No, keep walking. Act normal. I'm not here.
    -> What are you doing?
        Eve: Listening to the pipe. Alice and Bob haven't said a word to each other in three days. It's the most interesting thing in town.
    -> ⟨act normal⟩
<<endif>>
===

title: creator_intro
---
<<if condition("world.flag_set", "intro_raid_started")>>
    Creator: Not now! Stay close!
    -> ⟨fight⟩
<<else>>
    Creator: You're standing. Good. Walk to the bench and back, slowly. I want to hear the knees.
    -> Who are you?
        Creator: I built you. Mostly last night. The left knee came out of a filing cabinet.
    -> What am I for?
        Creator: I wrote that down. It's in one of the notebooks. Walk first, then we'll talk about it.
    -> What's that noise upstairs?
        Creator: Deliveries. I'm not expecting any.
    -> ⟨walk⟩
<<endif>>
===

title: gate_janitor_ripple
---
Gate Janitor: Mind the wet patch. Maintenance has this corridor today, so half the signs are turned around.
-> What's that shimmer?
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple__1>>
-> Where do the stable gates lead?
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple__2>>
-> What do you actually do?
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple__3>>
-> Who gets priority on a busy gate?
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple__priority>>
-> ⟨move on⟩
===

title: gate_janitor_ripple__1
---
Gate Janitor: Don't touch the shimmer. It won't take you anywhere. Gate Six works; use that if you need a gate.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple>>
-> ⟨move on⟩
===

title: gate_janitor_ripple__2
---
Gate Janitor: Six goes to a beach. Seven goes to some meeting room. Eight still says Tuesday. I stopped asking.
Gate Janitor: Seven's on the Math line now. Its breaker's on the wall; throw it and Seven dials TANGENT, and nothing else.
<<command "world.set_flag" "gate.known.TANGENT" true>>
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple>>
-> ⟨move on⟩
===

title: gate_janitor_ripple__3
---
Gate Janitor: Six jammed twice this morning. Seven leaks blue light. I'm here until both stop doing that.
Gate Janitor: And I mop. People walk out of a ring and lose breakfast. Robots never do. I like robots.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple>>
-> ⟨move on⟩
===

title: manifest_kiosk_wrong_list
---
Manifest Clerk: Name? ...No entry. Spell it again. Slower.
-> Can I go through the checkpoint?
    <<jump manifest_kiosk_wrong_list__1>>
-> What came through this morning?
    <<jump manifest_kiosk_wrong_list__2>>
-> Who else has the manifest?
    <<jump manifest_kiosk_wrong_list__copies>>
-> ⟨step away⟩
===

title: manifest_kiosk_wrong_list__1
---
Manifest Clerk: Manifested traffic only. You're not on the list. You're not on any list. I checked twice, which is once more than I'm paid for.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump manifest_kiosk_wrong_list>>
-> ⟨step away⟩
===

title: manifest_kiosk_wrong_list__2
---
Manifest Clerk: One crate, one lab of research, paid in advance, goblin carriers. Their papers were in order. Their spelling wasn't.
Manifest Clerk: It's in the freight yard behind the checkpoint, waiting for a gate. Next question.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump manifest_kiosk_wrong_list>>
-> ⟨step away⟩
===

title: gate_janitor_ripple__priority
---
Gate Janitor: Medical, if the dispatcher reads the red tag. Military, when they come down and tell him to move aside.
Gate Janitor: I watched a box of spare boots go through while a man waited with medicine for his kid. I told him to file a complaint. He laughed at me.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump gate_janitor_ripple>>
-> ⟨move on⟩
===

title: manifest_kiosk_wrong_list__copies
---
Manifest Clerk: We keep one copy here and one at the checkpoint. I corrected the basement address on ours.
Manifest Clerk: The checkpoint sent it back marked DENIED. That's all I can show you.
-> Ask another question.
    <<jump manifest_kiosk_wrong_list>>
-> ⟨step away⟩
===
